# Claude Code project tooling is VERSIONED, by ALLOWLIST: settings.json carries
# the hooks that block editing .env/.secret/.key and refuse `git push --force` /
# `rm -rf /`, and hooks/, agents/, commands/ and skills/ are the project's own
# tooling. A blanket ignore left the guard that protects this repo's credentials
# unversioned -- a fresh clone silently lost it.
#
# Allowlisted, not denylisted. The first attempt at narrowing named the three
# machine-local paths to ignore, which makes every FUTURE file any tool drops
# into .claude/ committed by default -- untenable in a public repo with a
# recorded credential exposure. Adding a new versioned path here is a
# deliberate one-line act; leaking one is now impossible by omission.
#
# `.claude/*` and not `.claude/`: git never descends into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a `!` line beneath `.claude/` could not re-include anything.
# Excluding the contents one by one is what makes the un-ignores below work.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/skills/
memory/

# Cookie/session files (per-user, contain JWTs)
.travian_cookies.json
.travian_persona.json
frontend/.travian_cookies.json
frontend/.travian_persona.json

